1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,166
If Earth stopped,

2
00:00:01,167 --> 00:00:02,466
you’d keep moving east—

3
00:00:02,467 --> 00:00:03,199
about a thousand

4
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:03,866
miles an hour

5
00:00:03,867 --> 00:00:04,700
at the equator.

6
00:00:04,767 --> 00:00:06,400
Loose objects keep going too.

7
00:00:06,533 --> 00:00:07,499
So does the air,

8
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:09,200
driving debris through the streets.

9
00:00:09,367 --> 00:00:10,699
And the ocean keeps moving

10
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:11,700
into the coast.

11
00:00:11,767 --> 00:00:12,999
You don’t feel the spin

12
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,300
because you move with Earth.

13
00:00:14,333 --> 00:00:15,467
Closer to the poles,

14
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,100
that starting speed is lower.

15
00:00:17,167 --> 00:00:18,767
The stop is imaginary.

16
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:20,500
The motion is real.

